  "worksAsStation": true,
  "description": "The coach shows one move: pulling the puck back through the legs, a toe drag (pulling the puck in with the tip of the blade), a spin-o-rama, a 360 or a heel-to-heel turn. In groups of three, one player carries the puck across the ice, makes the move on the way and leaves the puck for the next player, who brings it back. Change the move every few turns.",
  "steps": [
    "Coach shows one move first.",
    "Carry the puck across, make the move in the middle, and leave the puck for the next player.",
    "The next player picks it up and brings it back the same way."
  ],
